Big-Omega (Ω) Notation – Lower Bound
Big-Omega (Ω) notation represents the lower bound of an algorithm's time complexity. It defines the best-case scenario, meaning the minimum time an algorithm will always take, regardless of the input.

Definition
A function f(n) = Ω(g(n)) if there exist constants c > 0 and n0 such that:

